<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32907" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκστέφω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>take off the crown : empty</i> a full cup, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστέφω</span> (q.v.), <i><span class="en">
				Paus.Gr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				159
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>deck with garlands,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				171
			</span></i> ; esp. of suppliants, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκνα στολμοῖσι κρᾶτας ἐξεστεμμένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HF</u>
					526
				</span></i>
			 ; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκτηρίοις κλάδοισιν
				ἐξεστεμμένοι</span>
			<i>with garlands</i> on the suppliant olive-branches, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξέστεψε θάλασσαν</span>
			<i>he poured</i> it all round <i>like a garland,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.33
			</span></i>, cf. Sch. ; but better, <i>crowned,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφρύσι καὶ ῥηγμῖσι.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκστέψας: λόγον γυμνώσας,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>